#: cdbodialogs/CdboCopyCDDialog.cpp:213
msgid ""
"<br>"
"<br><b>Copy CD in Safe Mode:</b> In this mode process will first read out "
"source CD as an image file(s) to your hard drive and then burn it to target "
"CD-R(W). This mode decreases chance of buffer underruns. Working directory "
"must have sufficient space available to store image file(s). If not sure, "
"use this mode."
msgstr ""

#: cdbodialogs/CdboCopyCDDialog.cpp:217
msgid "Copy CD in Fast Mode"
msgstr ""

#: cdbodialogs/CdboCopyCDDialog.cpp:218
msgid ""
"<br>"
"<br><b>Copy CD in Fast Mode:</b>"
" Perform CD copy on the fly without creating an image file. Success of such "
"copy depends on your machine capabilities and system load. Higher system "
"load especially on weaker machines increases possibility of failure due to "
"buffer underruns. This is however the fastest way to copy CD."
msgstr ""

#: cdbodialogs/CdboCopyCDDialog.cpp:227
msgid "Force Copy"
msgstr ""

#: cdbodialogs/CdboCopyCDDialog.cpp:228
msgid ""
"<br>"
"<br><b>Force Copy:</b>"
" In this mode process will try to read out source Data CD even on some "
"errors. Use when Safe and Fast modes fail."
msgstr ""

